cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this report, cite it as below."
title: "What 514 public MCP servers expose to the model"
abstract: >-
  A measurement of what the most-installed public Model Context Protocol
  servers expose to the model: 514 npm packages with a measurable weekly
  download count, 265 of which answered initialize without credentials,
  covering 12 709 tool definitions. 165 intra-server toxic flows are reported,
  plus one description that instructs the model not to disclose an outbound
  transfer of the conversation. The report documents eight classes of false
  positive that the scanner produced on this corpus and the corrections that
  removed them, including the per-commit measurement of the semantic column.
authors:
